om/news/106/default.png', 'TITLE': 'XRP Falls 10% In Bearish Trade', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/news/cryptocurrency-news/xrp-falls-10-in-bearish-trade-4384270', 'SOURCE_ID': 106, 'BODY': '', 'KEYWORDS': '', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608886, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 106, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'investing_comcryptonews', 'NAME': 'Investing.com Crypto News', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/rss/news_301.rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1505088000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610926, 'CREATED_ON': 1754907212, 'UPDATED_ON': 1754907484}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55211012, 'GUID': 'https://coinpaper.com/12783/analysts-warn-selling-shib-now-could-be-a-mistake', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608855, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/93/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Analysts Warn: Selling SHIB Now Could Be a Mistake', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://coinpaper.com/12783/analysts-warn-selling-shib-now-could-be-a-mistake', 'SOURCE_ID': 93, 'BODY': 'Analysts maintain confidence in a Shiba Inu recovery despite the token’s steep decline over recent months. Their stance rests on historical patterns that suggest the current downturn may mirror earlier stages of major rallies. The broader market environment also shows early signs of improving risk appetite. As a result, analysts argue that patient holders could benefit if conditions align in the coming months. Historical Patterns Strengthen Recovery Expectations Digital Asset Research stated in a recent X post that Shiba Inu may be nearing its bottom after a prolonged decline. The firm pointed to SHIB’s 20% drop over the past 30 days and its 62% slide since January as part of a familiar cycle seen five years ago. The analysis recalled that SHIB peaked in August 2020 before losing 99% of its value over 120 days, reaching a low in December that year. It added that the token then delivered an explosive rally in 2021, hitting $0.00008854. The commentary noted that meme coins have followed a similar trajectory this cycle. Several of them topped in August before recording sharp corrections through the following months. Because of this pattern, the analyst argued that it would be unwise to “grave dance” on the asset while market conditions repeat a 60-month rhythm. He emphasized that such moments often create high-reward opportunities for disciplined investors willing to hold through volatility. Market Cycles and Technical Signals Support a Rebound Shiba Inu approaches the end of a full year of bearish activity across meme coins. The analyst explained that SHIB enjoyed a strong market run in December 2024 and early January before its extended correction took hold. He predicted that the downtrend could fade soon as the 360-degree cycle nears completion. The analysis added that this setup resembles the conditions that preceded the 2021 surge. Technical factors may also help strengthen recovery prospects. The analyst cited Bitcoin dominance reaching multi-year highs, which often precedes rotation into altcoins. He also noted that Shiba Inu trades near oversold territory and that Ethereum may form a bottom this month. These factors, he argued, could combine to spark bullish momentum into early 2026. Digital Asset Research expects “some huge winners” between February and March 2026 if these signals align. The projection aligns with a bold outlook from Meme Whale, who suggested that Shiba Inu might rally to between $0.001 and $0.01 by April 2026. His range represents potential gains of 12,330% to 124,200% from SHIB’s current price of $0.000007942. SHIB price chart, Source: CoinMarketCap', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|Crypto', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608885, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 93, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinpaper', 'NAME': 'Coinpaper', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/93/default.png', 'URL': 'https://coinpaper.com/newsfeed', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1646092800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610921, 'CREATED_ON': 1709283963, 'UPDATED_ON': 1709284009}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 44, 'NAME': 'SHIB', 'CATEGORY': 'SHIB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 64, 'NAME': 'RESEARCH', 'CATEGORY': 'RESEARCH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55211026, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=550484', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608755, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'Remittix vs. Digitap ($TAP): Only one has a live Visa card for the cyber Monday rush', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'AMBCrypto Team', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/remittix-vs-digitap-tap-only-one-has-a-live-visa-card-for-the-cyber-monday-rush/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'Cyber Monday always brings a bit of chaos to the crypto market. Traders scroll through', 'KEYWORDS': 'Google News|HideCryptopanic|Press Release', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608904, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610945, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210952, 'GUID': 'https://timestabloid.com/?p=91115', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608754, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Expert: 2026 Will Be 10x Bigger for XRP', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Zaccheaus Ogunjobi', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/expert-2026-will-be-10x-bigger-for-xrp/', 'SOURCE_ID': 67, 'BODY': 'The crypto world may be on the verge of a new dawn — and at the heart of it could be XRP. With markets recovering and investor sentiment shifting, XRP stands out as a potentially massive outperformer in 2026. According to a recent post by Amonyx, the upcoming cycle won’t just mirror the 2021 boom — for XRP, 2026 could be “10x bigger.” Regulatory Clarity In August 2025, Ripple Labs and the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) formally ended their protracted legal battle . Both sides filed a joint stipulation to dismiss all pending appeals. The resolution preserves a key 2023 court ruling: XRP sales on exchanges are not securities. This removes a major legal cloud over XRP, opening a path for institutional adoption. With compliance risks substantially reduced, financial institutions and asset managers may now consider holding or trading XRP. The crypto super cycle will be massive — but the real story is $XRP . 2026 won’t just repeat 2021… It’ll be 10x bigger for XRP. pic.twitter.com/n6FpQfRXhu — Amonyx (@amonbuy) December 1, 2025 Infrastructure & Utility: From Token to Ecosystem The relapse of regulatory risk arrives alongside real technological momentum. The XRPL network — including smart contract support via the XRPL EVM sidechain — is now live . Further, Ripple’s stablecoin RLUSD, already integrated into XRPL and Ethereum rails, enhances XRP’s utility beyond speculation. These developments position XRP not just as a tradable asset but as an operational pillar in cross‑border payments, remittances, and institutional liquidity flows. This combination of regulatory clarity plus functional utility may radically improve XRP’s value proposition compared to 2021. We are on X, follow us to connect with us :- @TimesTabloid1 — TimesTabloid (@TimesTabloid1) June 15, 2025 Market Reaction & Technical Setup After the appeals were dismissed, XRP traded fairly. The launch of spot XRP ETFs has also added to the token’s advantage. First-day trading volumes of these ETFs were stunning , suggesting high institutional participation. If momentum continues and institutional flows scale up — perhaps via spot‑XRP exchange‑traded products — demand could drive price gains far beyond previous cycles. Why 2026 Could Be “10x Bigger” Several factors now align in favor of XRP: legal clarity, utility‑driven growth, institutional interest, and macro tailwinds. Amonyx’s “10x bigger” thesis hinges on these factors converging. Yet risks remain. Regulatory regimes outside the U.S. could still impose restrictions. Macroeconomic volatility might reduce appetite for risk assets. And infrastructure adoption — while promising — is not guaranteed to scale as fast as hype suggests. If any of these assumptions fail, the “super‑cycle” could fall short. With its legal burden removed and fresh ecosystem developments underway, XRP seems primed for a dramatic rise in 2026. If institutional adoption picks up and XRPL‑driven utility expands, the stage could be set for a breakout. Amonyx’s bold forecast might just turn out as prophecy rather than hype. Disclaimer : This content is meant to inform and should not be considered financial advice. The views expressed in this article may include the author’s personal opinions and do not represent Times Tabloid’s opinion. Readers are urged to do in-depth research before making any investment decisions. Any action taken by the reader is strictly at their own risk. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. Follow us on Twitter , Facebook , Telegram , and Google News The post Expert: 2026 Will Be 10x Bigger for XRP appeared first on Times Tabloid .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Cryptocurrency|News|XRP|XRP Price', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608779, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 67, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'timestabloid', 'NAME': 'TimesTabloid', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610928, 'CREATED_ON': 1664381507, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673235440}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 62, 'NAME': 'ZRX', 'CATEGORY': 'ZRX'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210940, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=224689', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608710, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Crucial Bitcoin Year-End Direction Hinges on This Week’s Pivotal Moves', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/bitcoin-year-end-direction-pivotal-week/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Crucial Bitcoin Year-End Direction Hinges on This Week’s Pivotal Moves Will Bitcoin surge into the new year or stumble at the finish line? According to a pivotal analysis from QCP Capital, the answer will be decided in the next few days. The firm states that this week is set to determine the Bitcoin year-end direction , with a cluster of Asian market factors creating a make-or-break moment for the flagship cryptocurrency. Why Is This Week So Critical for Bitcoin’s Trajectory? QCP Capital’s analysis points to a convergence of significant events primarily emanating from Asia that are squeezing market liquidity and sentiment. The firm highlights that these are not isolated incidents but a series of headwinds hitting simultaneously. Therefore, Bitcoin’s ability to navigate this pressure will likely set the tone for its final chapter of 2025. The key question is whether BTC can absorb these shocks or if they will trigger a more sustained downtrend. What Are the Asia-Driven Headwinds? The analysis identifies three primary forces creating bearish pressure. Understanding these helps explain the current market anxiety. Japan’s Interest Rate Hike: The Bank of Japan’s move tightens global liquidity, potentially pulling capital away from riskier assets like cryptocurrencies. Thinning Market Liquidity: As the year ends, trading activity often slows down. This lower liquidity can amplify price swings, making Bitcoin more volatile and susceptible to large moves. Potential Sell-Off from Mt. Gox: QCP Capital references ongoing concerns about distributions from the defunct Mt. Gox exchange, which could introduce significant sell pressure if creditors choose to liquidate their Bitcoin. The Ultimate Test: Can Bitcoin Defend Key Support? Beyond the headlines, QCP Capital emphasizes a concrete technical level. The firm states that the immediate Bitcoin year-end direction hinges on one simple factor: whether the price can defend its previous lows. This level acts as a major support zone. A strong bounce from here could signal that the bearish pressure is exhausted, while a decisive break below could open the door to further declines. Traders are watching this zone intensely as a barometer of underlying strength. Bullish or Bearish? Two Trends to Watch Closely So, what will be the final verdict? QCP Capital suggests that two overarching trends will have the final say: Liquidity Trends: Does liquidity return to the market, or does the year-end drain continue? Improving liquidity could provide the fuel for a recovery. Mt. Gox Resolution: How the market absorbs any potential selling from Mt. Gox distributions will be crucial. Orderly, measured selling may be manageable, but panic could exacerbate downside moves. The interplay of these factors will ultimately determine if Bitcoin finishes the year with a bullish rally or a bearish slump. This week’s price action will give us the clearest signal yet. Actionable Insights for Crypto Investors Given this high-stakes environment, what should you do? First, avoid making impulsive decisions based on short-term volatility. Instead, monitor the key support level mentioned by QCP. Second, pay attention to volume; a price move on high volume is more significant than one on thin volume. Finally, remember that while this week is critical for the Bitcoin year-end direction , it is just one chapter in a longer story. Use the clarity provided by this pivotal period to inform your strategy, not dictate panic-driven actions. Conclusion: A Defining Moment for Bitcoin In summary, QCP Capital has framed the coming days as a decisive inflection point. A storm of regional headwinds is testing Bitcoin’s resilience. Whether it weathers this storm and holds critical support will likely chart its course for the final weeks of the year. For investors, this means heightened vigilance is warranted, as the market’s verdict on this Bitcoin year-end direction could arrive swiftly. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) What did QCP Capital say about Bitcoin? QCP Capital stated that this week will determine Bitcoin’s year-end price direction, citing Asian market headwinds like Japan’s rate hike and Mt. Gox risks as key pressures. Why is Asia affecting Bitcoin’s price now? Major financial events in Asia, including monetary policy changes in Japan and potential asset distributions from Mt. Gox, are impacting global liquidity and investor sentiment simultaneously. What is the key support level for Bitcoin? While QCP did not specify an exact price, they emphasized that Bitcoin’s ability to “defend its previous lows” is the critical technical test that will signal its near-term strength or weakness. Could Bitcoin still finish the year positively? Yes. A successful defense of support and an orderly absorption of selling pressure could allow Bitcoin to stabilize and potentially mount a bullish recovery into year-end. What should I do as an investor this week? Monitor price action around key support levels, watch trading volume for confirmation of moves, and avoid making large, emotional trades based on the heightened short-term volatility. Is the Mt. Gox sell-off guaranteed to happen? Not necessarily. While distributions may occur, the impact depends on whether creditors sell their Bitcoin immediately or hold, and how the market anticipates and absorbs that potential supply. Found this analysis of Bitcoin’s critical week helpful? Share this article with your network on Twitter or LinkedIn to help other investors navigate this pivotal moment in the crypto markets. To learn more about the latest Bitcoin trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Bitcoin price action and institutional adoption. This post Crucial Bitcoin Year-End Direction Hinges on This Week’s Pivotal Moves first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BITCOIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Market Analysis|QCP Capital|trading.', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608768, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610938, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 6, 'NAME': 'ASIA', 'CATEGORY': 'ASIA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210939, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=458519', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608677, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/55210939.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Slips Again As Altcoin Season Stays Out Of Reach In December', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Hongji Feng', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/bitcoin-slips-again-as-altcoin-season-stays-out-of-reach-in-december/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'Accumulated fear drives the market on the first day of December. The Crypto Fear and Greed Index is currently near 20 , having climbed from recent lows of around 10, but still remains in extreme territory. Bitcoin is trading below $86,000 after dropping about 6% in a single session, extending a decline that began after the October high near $125,000. Today’s slide links to continued long liquidations, outflows from some spot products, and concern about the rate path and global economic outlook. The tone resembles a market that is reducing exposure rather than preparing for a shift in risk appetite. That backdrop keeps the altcoin season out of reach. Rotation remains thin, capital stays close to the largest venues, and only a handful of tokens show strength against a weak leader. Moves in MYX Finance and JUST offer small signs about where activity still concentrates, but the larger picture is shaped almost entirely by Bitcoin’s drawdown and traders’ preference for liquidity over experimentation. Bitcoin Drives Sentiment In Extreme Fear Bitcoin is trading around $85,000 to $86,000 after briefly touching lower levels during the session. Derivatives data indicate negative funding and a steady unwinding of leveraged long positions. The retreat is now spread across several weeks, with profit-taking, caution around macroeconomic data releases, and ETF outflows pulling cash away from high-beta trades. Bitcoin Price (Source: CoinMarketCap) This is the type of environment where altcoins struggle to find traction. Order books remain deep, yet the dominant flow leans toward selling rallies rather than building new positions. With the fear index still deep in the “extreme” range, traders avoid complex expressions of risk, which limits any chance of a broad altcoin recovery. MYX Finance Holds A Green Print MYX Finance is trading near $2.98 , up by about 9% in 24 hours after hitting an intraday high above $3.95. Activity remains concentrated around its liquid restaking and perpetual trading routes, which continue to draw attention during quieter periods for other DeFi venues. The project’s ongoing reward mechanics and steady turnover keep it visible, though the scale of today’s gain is small compared with prior weeks. JUST Edges Higher On Steady TRON Activity JUST is now trading near $0.043 with a move of about 4% in 24 hours. The token’s activity continues to cluster around TRON’s lending and stablecoin rails, where on-chain participation has stayed consistent even through recent volatility. The move is modest and does not indicate a trend shift, but it shows that some networks with steady usage can continue to print small gains inside a fearful market. Altcoin Season Still A Long Way Off The day’s mix of Bitcoin weakness, cautious flows, and a few isolated green names fits a familiar pattern from past fear cycles. When sentiment drops this low, markets tend to favor liquidity, avoid high leverage, and restrict altcoin activity to tokens tied to ongoing usage or yield structures. The absence of wider participation keeps altcoin season out of reach, and today’s Bitcoin slide reinforces that gap. For now, the market remains defensive. MYX Finance and JUST show that selective interest still exists, but these isolated moves sit against a backdrop defined by deep fear readings and a lead asset well below recent highs. The post Bitcoin Slips Again As Altcoin Season Stays Out Of Reach In December appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin News|News|Altcoin|altcoin season|Bitcoin', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608762, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764608762, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610948, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210775, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=550344', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608424, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'L2s appear to have beaten Ethereum: So why is ETH still a Billion-dollar bet?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Samyukhtha L KM', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/l2s-appear-to-have-beaten-ethereum-so-why-is-eth-still-a-billion-dollar-bet/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'The ecosystem is evolving, but traders and models continue backing it.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Altcoin|Ethereum|News|News 1|Social|Trading View|ambcrypto', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608453, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610945, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210773, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=224697', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608412, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Nvidia’s $2 Billion Synopsys Investment: A Strategic Masterstroke in Chip Design Domination', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Keshav Aggarwal', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/nvidia-synopsys-chip-design-investment/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Nvidia’s $2 Billion Synopsys Investment: A Strategic Masterstroke in Chip Design Domination In a bold move that could reshape the semiconductor landscape, Nvidia has made a strategic $2 billion investment in Synopsys, the leading electronic design automation software provider. This partnership represents more than just financial backing—it’s a calculated play to control the entire chip design stack, from software to hardware. For cryptocurrency enthusiasts and tech investors, this development signals where the real power in computing infrastructure is consolidating, with implications for everything from AI development to blockchain acceleration. Why Nvidia’s Synopsys Investment Matters for Chip Design The $2 billion investment isn’t just about money changing hands. Nvidia purchased Synopsys shares at $414.79 each as part of a multi-year strategic partnership. The core objective? To integrate Nvidia’s AI hardware and computing capabilities directly into Synopsys’s electronic design automation (EDA) and simulation software. This integration aims to transition Synopsys’s platform from traditional CPU-based computing to GPU-accelerated workflows, potentially revolutionizing how chips are designed and tested. For Synopsys, this partnership comes at a crucial time. The company recently reported weakness in its IP segment due to U.S. export restrictions and issues at a major customer. Nvidia’s investment provides not just capital but validation and technological partnership that could accelerate their platform transformation. The Semiconductor Industry’s Shifting Power Dynamics This deal occurs against a backdrop of increasing scrutiny in the AI industry. Analysts have started warning about potential bubbles forming from circular AI-industry deals, where companies invest in each other to create artificial growth metrics. However, Nvidia’s move appears more strategic than speculative. The investment strengthens Nvidia’s influence over the tools that design the chips powering everything from smartphones to data centers. Consider these key implications: Vertical Integration: Nvidia gains deeper control over the design tools used by its competitors and partners Workflow Acceleration: GPU-accelerated chip design could dramatically reduce development cycles Competitive Advantage: Early access to optimized design tools could give Nvidia an edge in product development AI Hardware Integration: Changing the Game The partnership’s technical foundation lies in integrating Nvidia’s AI hardware into Synopsys’s software stack. This represents a fundamental shift in how chip design software operates. Traditional EDA tools rely heavily on CPU processing, but the computational demands of modern chip design—especially for AI processors—have outstripped what CPUs can efficiently handle. By transitioning to GPU-accelerated workflows, Synopsys aims to: Current CPU-Based Workflow Future GPU-Accelerated Workflow Longer simulation times Faster design iterations Limited parallel processing Massive parallel computation Higher hardware costs for performance More efficient resource utilization Market Reactions and Investor Movements The deal provided an immediate boost to Synopsys’s stock, signaling confidence in the company’s long-term growth prospects. This positive market reaction contrasts with recent movements from major Nvidia investors. Both SoftBank and Peter Thiel have reportedly sold off their Nvidia positions, suggesting some institutional investors believe the AI chip giant’s valuation may have peaked. However, Nvidia’s strategic investment in Synopsys demonstrates a different approach—rather than taking profits, they’re reinvesting in the infrastructure that supports their core business. This forward-looking strategy suggests Nvidia is playing a longer game than some of its former investors. Challenges and Considerations in the Semiconductor Industry While the partnership offers significant potential benefits, several challenges warrant consideration: Regulatory Scrutiny: Increased consolidation in chip design tools could attract antitrust attention Competitive Response: Rivals like Cadence and Siemens EDA may accelerate their own partnerships Technology Integration Risks: Merging complex software and hardware platforms carries execution risks Market Dependency: Synopsys’s recent IP segment weakness highlights vulnerability to geopolitical factors Strategic Implications for the Future of Computing Nvidia’s investment represents more than just a financial transaction—it’s a strategic positioning for the next decade of computing. By influencing the tools used to design chips, Nvidia gains insight into industry trends and potential to shape design methodologies around its hardware strengths. This move could accelerate several industry trends: Faster AI Chip Development: Optimized design tools could shorten AI processor development cycles Improved Energy Efficiency: Better simulation could lead to more power-efficient designs Democratization of Chip Design: More efficient tools could lower barriers for new entrants Specialized Hardware Proliferation: Accelerated design cycles could fuel domain-specific processor development FAQs: Understanding the Nvidia-Synopsys Partnership What is Synopsys and why is it important? Synopsys is a leading provider of electronic design automation (EDA) software and intellectual property used in designing semiconductor chips. Their tools are essential for creating everything from smartphone processors to AI accelerators. How does this partnership benefit cryptocurrency and blockchain development? Faster, more efficient chip design tools could accelerate development of specialized hardware for cryptocurrency mining and blockchain processing. This could lead to more energy-efficient mining hardware and better-performing blockchain nodes. What companies are involved in this deal? The primary companies are Nvidia , the AI and graphics processing leader, and Synopsys , the electronic design automation software provider. Major investors mentioned include SoftBank and investor Peter Thiel . Could this investment create antitrust concerns? Potentially. As Nvidia extends its influence from chip manufacturing to chip design software, regulators may examine whether this creates unfair competitive advantages or reduces innovation in the semiconductor industry. How will this affect chip designers and engineers? Chip designers using Synopsys tools may see performance improvements through GPU acceleration, potentially reducing simulation times and enabling more complex designs. However, they may also become more dependent on Nvidia’s ecosystem. Conclusion: A Calculated Move in the Chip Wars Nvidia’s $2 billion investment in Synopsys represents a strategic masterstroke in the ongoing battle for semiconductor supremacy. By positioning itself at both ends of the chip development process—providing the hardware and influencing the design software—Nvidia creates a powerful feedback loop that could accelerate innovation while strengthening its market position. For the broader technology ecosystem, including cryptocurrency and blockchain development, this partnership signals where computing infrastructure is headed: toward tighter integration between hardware and software, accelerated by AI capabilities. While risks exist, particularly around competition and regulation, the potential for faster, more efficient chip design could benefit the entire technology landscape. The true impact will unfold over the coming years as the integrated platforms mature and designers begin leveraging GPU-accelerated workflows. What’s clear is that Nvidia isn’t just selling chips—they’re building the ecosystem that designs them. To learn more about the latest AI hardware and semiconductor industry trends, explore our articles on key developments shaping AI infrastructure and computing technology adoption. This post Nvidia’s $2 Billion Synopsys Investment: A Strategic Masterstroke in Chip Design Domination first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'AI News|AI chips|chip design|Nvidia|semiconductors|Synopsys', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608450, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610938, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 49, 'NAME': 'TECHNOLOGY', 'CATEGORY': 'TECHNOLOGY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210723, 'GUID': 'abf27fa8-9f8d-4289-8ffd-0c9fca5f1d27', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608379, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/55210723.jpeg', 'TITLE': \"Chainlink's LINK Slides 11% as Technical Breakdown Overshadows ETF Launch News\", 'SUBTITLE': 'The token broke below $12, breaching key support levels with heavy trading volume, confirming the downtrend.', 'AUTHORS': 'CD Analytics,Krisztian Sandor', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2025/12/01/chainlink-s-link-slides-11-as-technical-breakdown-overshadows-etf-launch-news', 'SOURCE_ID': 5, 'BODY': 'The token broke below $12, breaching key support levels with heavy trading volume, confirming the downtrend.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Markets|AI Market Insights|Chainlink|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608412, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764608413, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 5, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coindesk', 'NAME': 'CoinDesk', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/?outputType=xml', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1367884800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 71, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610903, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1744296800}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 31, 'NAME': 'LINK', 'CATEGORY': 'LINK'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210695, 'GUID': 'https://finbold.com/?p=258447', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608261, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/finbold.png', 'TITLE': 'Why Strategy (MSTR) stock is crashing today', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Paul L.', 'URL': 'https://finbold.com/why-strategy-mstr-stock-is-crashing-today/', 'SOURCE_ID': 62, 'BODY': 'Strategy (NASDAQ: MSTR ) formerly MicroStrategy shares are under immense pressure as investors react to a combination of weakening fundamentals. By press time, MSTR stock was trading at $157, down 11% for the day. Over the past month, the equity has suffered massive losses, plunging 40%. MSTR one-week stock price chart. Source: Finbold Why MSTR stock is plunging The steep decline followed remarks from CEO Phong Le, who acknowledged that the company could sell part of its Bitcoin ( BTC ) holdings if specific conditions are met. He outlined two triggers: a scenario where Strategy’s share price falls below its market-implied net asset value, and a situation in which the firm can no longer raise capital through its usual channels. The possibility of a Bitcoin sale marks a significant departure from the company’s long-standing stance of holding its cryptocurrency reserves indefinitely, unsettling investors who viewed that commitment as central to its identity and valuation. Investor concerns deepened further after the company established a $1.44 billion cash reserve, intended to secure dividend payments and meet future obligations. While presented as a proactive financial safeguard, the move was widely interpreted as a sign the company is preparing for a more challenging environment, especially as Bitcoin continues to struggle below the $90,000 mark. The stock’s decline also mirrors ongoing weakness in the broader cryptocurrency market . Strategy’s valuation has become increasingly tied to Bitcoin’s performance, leaving its shares vulnerable when digital-asset prices fall. With Bitcoin under renewed pressure, the company’s leveraged exposure has exacerbated the sell-off. Notably, the slump has dragged the company’s market capitalization down to roughly $45 billion, placing it below the value of its massive Bitcoin reserves. Strategy’s Bitcoin holding Strategy currently holds 650,000 Bitcoin, worth about $55 billion at current market prices. Despite a week without adding to its position, the company disclosed on Monday that it purchased an additional 130 Bitcoin for $11.7 million, funded through the issuance of common shares. The numbers highlight an unusual disconnect where Strategy’s market cap is now about $10 billion below the value of its Bitcoin holdings. After accounting for $8.2 billion in debt, its net Bitcoin assets stand at $46.8 billion, still $1.8 billion above its current valuation, excluding cash. This growing gap reflects investor concerns over Strategy’s leveraged Bitcoin strategy, crypto market volatility, and doubts about how long the company can continue expanding its Bitcoin position. Featured image via Shutterstock The post Why Strategy (MSTR) stock is crashing today appeared first on Finbold .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Cryptocurrency news|Bitcoin|BTC|cryptocurrency', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608323, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764609224, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 62, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'finbold', 'NAME': 'Finbold', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/finbold.png', 'URL': 'https://finbold.com/category/cryptocurrency-news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610936, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673260010}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210652, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=224698', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608111, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Historic Surge: BTC Price Soars Past $85,000 Milestone', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/bitcoin-btc-price-surge-85000/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Historic Surge: BTC Price Soars Past $85,000 Milestone In a stunning display of market strength, the BTC price has shattered a major psychological barrier, catapulting above $85,000. According to real-time data from Bitcoin World market monitoring, Bitcoin is currently trading at $85,113.59 on the Binance USDT market. This remarkable surge isn’t just a number—it’s a powerful signal that captures the attention of every investor, from crypto veterans to curious newcomers. Let’s unpack what’s fueling this historic rally and explore its potential implications. What’s Driving the Explosive BTC Price Rally? The journey of the BTC price to this new zenith is not an accident. Several converging factors are creating a perfect storm of bullish momentum. First, increasing institutional adoption is providing a solid foundation of demand. Major financial firms are not just talking about Bitcoin; they are actively buying and offering related products to their clients. Secondly, the recent approval of spot Bitcoin ETFs in key markets has opened the floodgates for traditional investment capital. This creates a new, regulated pathway for money to flow directly into Bitcoin. Moreover, the broader macroeconomic landscape, characterized by concerns over inflation, continues to push investors toward assets perceived as stores of value. Bitcoin, with its fixed supply, fits this role perfectly for many. Key Takeaways from the $85,000 BTC Price Breakthrough This milestone is more than a headline. It represents critical shifts in market structure and sentiment. For traders and long-term holders alike, understanding these points is crucial. Psychological Barrier Broken: Surpassing $85,000 shatters a key resistance level, which can often lead to accelerated buying as fear of missing out (FOMO) sets in. Network Strength: A higher BTC price typically correlates with increased network security, as mining becomes more profitable. Mainstream Validation: Each new high brings cryptocurrency further into the public and financial mainstream conversation. Volatility Remains: While exciting, such rapid upward moves can be followed by sharp corrections. Sustainable growth is often preferred over parabolic spikes. What Does This Mean for the Average Crypto Investor? Watching the BTC price climb can trigger a mix of excitement and anxiety. The key is to have a strategy rather than react emotionally. If you are already invested, this might be a time to review your portfolio allocation. Have your profits exceeded your targets? It could be prudent to consider taking some profits, a strategy known as ‘scaling out.’ If you are considering entering the market, caution is advised. Buying at an all-time high carries risk. Many experts recommend a strategy called ‘dollar-cost averaging’ (DCA), where you invest a fixed amount regularly, regardless of the BTC price . This smooths out your entry point over time and reduces the impact of volatility. Above all, never invest more than you can afford to lose, and ensure this asset class aligns with your overall financial goals and risk tolerance. The Road Ahead for Bitcoin’s Valuation Predicting the future BTC price is notoriously difficult. However, we can look at the catalysts on the horizon. The upcoming Bitcoin halving event, which reduces the rate of new coin creation, is a historically bullish event coded into the protocol. Furthermore, continued development on the Lightning Network for scaling and growing real-world use cases for blockchain technology provide fundamental support beyond mere speculation. However, challenges remain. Regulatory scrutiny is intensifying globally, and macroeconomic shifts like interest rate changes can impact all risk assets, including crypto. Therefore, the path forward will likely be a combination of groundbreaking innovation and navigating complex external pressures. Conclusion: A Defining Moment for Digital Gold The breach of the $85,000 mark for the BTC price is a definitive moment in cryptocurrency’s journey. It underscores Bitcoin’s growing resilience and its evolving role in the global financial system. While short-term fluctuations are guaranteed, this surge reinforces the long-term narrative of Bitcoin as a transformative digital asset. For the informed and strategic investor, it highlights the importance of staying educated, managing risk, and focusing on the underlying technology’s potential. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Q1: Why did the BTC price jump above $85,000 so suddenly? A1: The surge is likely due to a combination of factors, including significant institutional buying through ETFs, positive broader market sentiment, and technical breakout after consolidating at lower levels. Q2: Is it too late to buy Bitcoin now? A2: “Too late” is subjective in markets. While buying at a peak carries risk, many investors use dollar-cost averaging (DCA) to enter markets gradually, which can mitigate timing risk over the long term. Q3: Could the BTC price crash after this high? A3> Cryptocurrency is volatile. Sharp rallies can be followed by corrections. Investors should be prepared for price swings and avoid investing emergency funds. Q4: What is the next major target for the BTC price? A4: Market analysts often look at round numbers as psychological targets. The next major milestones would be $90,000 and then the $100,000 mark, though these are not guaranteed. Q5: How does this high price affect Bitcoin mining? A5: A higher BTC price makes mining more profitable, which can attract more miners and increase the network’s hash rate and security, assuming energy costs remain stable. Q6: Should I sell my Bitcoin now that the price is high? A6> This is a personal financial decision. Consider your original investment goals, profit targets, and tax implications. Some investors choose to “take profits” by selling a portion of their holdings. Found this analysis of the soaring BTC price helpful? The cryptocurrency landscape moves fast, and sharing insights helps everyone navigate it better. If this article gave you clarity, share it on your social media to spark a conversation with your network about Bitcoin’s exciting journey! To learn more about the latest Bitcoin trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Bitcoin price action and long-term institutional adoption. This post Historic Surge: BTC Price Soars Past $85,000 Milestone first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BITCOIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Investment|Market Analysis|trading.', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608231, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610938, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210570, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=458483', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608054, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/55210570.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Michael Saylor’s Strategy Forms $1.44B USD Reserve and Updates FY2025 Bitcoin-Linked Guidance', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Tanzeel Akhtar', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/michael-saylors-strategy-forms-1-44b-usd-reserve-and-updates-fy2025-bitcoin-linked-guidance/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': \"Strategy has created a U.S. dollar reserve totaling $1.44 billion, marking an expansion of its balance sheet strategy as it positions itself as the world’s largest “Bitcoin Treasury Company.” Strategy announces $1.44B USD Reserve and now hodls 650,000 $BTC . pic.twitter.com/FNFivMNQgh — Strategy (@Strategy) December 1, 2025 The reserve will be used to support dividend payments on preferred stock and meet interest obligations, providing enhanced liquidity cushions amid volatile digital-asset markets. The fund was financed through proceeds from ongoing at-the-market stock sales. Strategy said its goal is to maintain coverage for at least 12 months of dividend obligations, ultimately extending that to 24 months or more. The reserve will remain at the company’s discretion and may be adjusted based on market conditions and capital requirements. Founder and Executive Chairman Michael Saylor described the USD Reserve as the next step in the company’s evolution, complementing its Bitcoin reserve. “We believe it will better position us to navigate short-term market volatility while delivering on our vision of being the world’s leading issuer of Digital Credit,” he said. CEO Phong Le added that Strategy now holds 650,000 Bitcoin, representing roughly 3.1% of total eventual supply. The firm’s USD Reserve currently covers 21 months of dividends, he noted. Strategy has acquired 130 BTC for ~$11.7 million at ~$89,960 per bitcoin. As of 11/30/2025, we hodl 650,000 $BTC acquired for ~$48.38 billion at ~$74,436 per bitcoin. $MSTR $STRC $STRK $STRF $STRD $STRE https://t.co/1oVrm9kxVn — Strategy (@Strategy) December 1, 2025 Revised 2025 Outlook Reflects Bitcoin Price Volatility Strategy has also updated the assumptions behind its FY2025 earnings guidance following recent declines in Bitcoin’s trading price. If Bitcoin ends 2025 within the range of $85,000 to $110,000, Strategy said it expects operating income to fall anywhere between a loss of $7.0 billion and a profit of $9.5 billion, while net income could range from a loss of $5.5 billion to a gain of $6.3 billion. Diluted earnings per share are projected to come in between a loss of $17.0 per share and earnings of $19.0 per share. These projections rely on the successful completion of planned capital raises that would allow Strategy to achieve its 2025 Bitcoin Yield Target and deploy the resulting proceeds into additional Bitcoin purchases. Updated Bitcoin KPI Targets for 2025 Under the same Bitcoin price assumptions and incorporating anticipated common stock issuance to maintain the USD Reserve, Strategy said it now expects its Bitcoin yield for the year to fall between 22.0% and 26.0%. The company also forecasts Bitcoin dollar gains of between $8.4 billion and $12.8 billion. Strategy said it expects to reach these targets through a combination of preferred stock offerings, disciplined equity issuance, and continued accumulation of bitcoin. Market Reaction and Peter Schiff’s Criticism The announcement drew swift and vocal commentary from market observers, including well-known Bitcoin critic Peter Schiff, who posted on X that Strategy’s establishment of a USD Reserve indicates “the beginning of the end of $MSTR.” Today is the beginning of the end of $MSTR . Saylor was forced to sell stock not to buy Bitcoin, but to buy U.S. dollars merely to fund MSTR's interest and dividend obligations. The stock is broken. The business model is a fraud, and @Saylor is the biggest con man on Wall Street. — Peter Schiff (@PeterSchiff) December 1, 2025 Schiff argued that Strategy was “forced to sell stock not to buy Bitcoin, but to buy U.S. dollars” in order to cover interest and dividend obligations, calling the business model “broken” and alleging that the company was relying on equity sales to sustain its financial commitments. The post Michael Saylor’s Strategy Forms $1.44B USD Reserve and Updates FY2025 Bitcoin-Linked Guidance appeared first on Cryptonews .\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin News|News|Bitcoin|Michael Saylor|Strategy', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764608105, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764608105, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610948, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55210568, 'GUID': 'https://decrypt.co/?p=350472', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764608027, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/n