tcoin-led-selloff-hits-us-crypto-stocks-as-mstr-bmnr-and-coinbase-plunge-over-10', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764605275, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/55209476.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin-Led Selloff Hits US Crypto Stocks as MSTR, BMNR and Coinbase Plunge Over 10%', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/breakingnews/bitcoin-led-selloff-hits-us-crypto-stocks-as-mstr-bmnr-and-coinbase-plunge-over-10', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin-Led Selloff Hits US Crypto Stocks as MSTR, BMNR and Coinbase Plunge Over 10%', 'KEYWORDS': 'Breaking News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764606158, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764606159, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610915, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55209675, 'GUID': 'https://blockworks.co/news/yen-pressures', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764605161, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/blockworks.png', 'TITLE': 'Yen pressures meet soft crypto carry', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://blockworks.co/news/yen-pressures', 'SOURCE_ID': 55, 'BODY': 'BTC’s Asia-session move and Ethena’s weaker yields reflect a market adjusting to tighter yen funding and softer derivatives carry', 'KEYWORDS': '0xResearch Newsletter', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764606547, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 55, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'blockworks', 'NAME': 'Blockworks', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/blockworks.png', 'URL': 'https://blockworks.co/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1610236800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 59, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610903, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1737815987}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55208917, 'GUID': 'https://timestabloid.com/?p=91108', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764605158, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Over\\u202f40,000 Abnormal XRP Transactions Appear Out of Nowhere. Here’s What Happened', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Zaccheaus Ogunjobi', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/over-40000-abnormal-xrp-transactions-appear-out-of-nowhere-heres-what-happened/', 'SOURCE_ID': 67, 'BODY': 'The XRP Ledger (XRPL) recently recorded a surge of more than 40,000 AccountSet transactions in a narrow time window. This spike was flagged by a well‑known XRPL contributor, who emphasized its volume and organization. Analysts noted the abrupt increase landed in the 20,000–40,000 transactions range. That pattern matches what you would expect when someone designs, configures, and readies a large batch of wallets — perhaps for institutional use, not everyday users. Because AccountSet does not move value but instead configures accounts — setting flags, updating keys, enabling permissions — this volume suggests a large‑scale infrastructure setup. The ledger event has raised immediate questions: who initiated it, and for what purpose? Why Does This Surge Look Different? In the past, the most significant bulk‑account irregularity on XRPL was linked to BitGo. In that incident, a flawed script triggered repeated “unfunded payment” errors while trying to activate new wallets. The issue caused thousands of failed transactions and account sprawl. The current wave differs markedly. Instead of payment failures and errors, the ledgers show clean, controlled AccountSet transactions. The scale is also larger. The structure and consistency suggest deliberate orchestration and not a runaway script. This contrast underscores why many in the XRPL community interpret the surge as intentional infrastructure preparation — not a bug. Someone is doing a lot of AccountSet TXs on the XRP Ledger recently. Even after BitGo stopped. pic.twitter.com/rhdYGqFzLr — Vet (@Vet_X0) November 29, 2025 XRPL Growth and Network‑Wide Activity Surge The surge comes at a time of notable expansion for XRPL . The number of accounts holding at least the minimum balance recently surpassed 7\\u202fmillion, per a leading ledger‑explorer report. Meanwhile, daily interacting addresses have skyrocketed. Over a recent week, XRPL saw roughly 295,000 active addresses daily — about seven times the prior three‑month average of 35,000–40,000. The growth in new accounts also remains strong. At one point, XRPL recorded 21,595 new wallets within 48 hours — the fastest rate in eight months. Yet even with this growth, such a concentrated AccountSet spike had never been documented at this scale. Normal growth usually shows up across payments, simple transfers, or ordinary wallet creations — not tens of thousands of configuration transactions clustered tightly in time. What This Might Signal Because AccountSet is used for configuration — such as adjusting account flags, updating keys, or enabling permissions — a surge of this magnitude may represent a preparatory phase. That could involve setting up a large wallet cluster ready to receive funds, tokens, or stablecoins. Another possibility: a large actor is re‑structuring their wallets behind the scenes — rearranging holdings, consolidating accounts, or preparing new wallet architecture ahead of major operations. Alternatively, this could indicate pre‑launch infrastructure for new services — perhaps custodial wallets, stablecoin platforms, or institutional liquidity pools. The timing might coincide with broader demand for XRPL-based products. However, it is important to stress: the public data does not yet reveal who is behind this wave. There are no known identities tied to these transactions, and no declarations from institutions or custodians. We are on X, follow us to connect with us :- @TimesTabloid1 — TimesTabloid (@TimesTabloid1) June 15, 2025 Concurrent Exchange Flows Add Complexity to The Picture Alongside the ledger‑level activity, public reports suggest significant XRP movement across key exchanges. According to those sources, one major exchange reportedly saw over 68\\u202fmillion XRP leave over seven days, and more than 35\\u202fmillion XRP across the prior month. At the same time, other exchanges reportedly documented strong inflows. This pattern suggests funds are being redistributed among exchanges or custodial platforms at the same moment ledger‑level preparations intensify. The juxtaposition of heavy back‑end configuration and large exchange flows deepens the mystery — it might point to coordinated institutional activity, or simply simultaneous but unrelated events. What to Watch Next The community is now watching for follow‑up signals. If the wave represents genuine infrastructure deployment, the next steps may include large XRP deposits into the newly configured wallets. We might also see activation of trust lines, feature flags, or metadata signaling readiness for token issuance or stablecoin operations. Another potential sign is bulk movements between wallets — particularly between long‑dormant accounts and new clusters. Or a stream of deposits into major exchanges, followed by outflows toward private wallets. If these emerge, they could clarify whether this is a precursor to major liquidity deployment, institutional onboarding, or simply internal wallet re‑organization. A Major Signal in XRPL — Intriguing But Not Yet Decisive The sudden appearance of over 40,000 AccountSet transactions within a short span marks one of the most unusual ledger events in XRPL history. It stands out from regular traffic, from prior wallet‑creation surges, and from previous glitches like the BitGo incident. While the wave strongly suggests some deliberate, large‑scale setup — perhaps for institutional use or infrastructure deployment — current public data does not confirm who triggered it nor what their endgame is. For now, this surge remains a compelling but open question in the XRPL ecosystem. What happens next — wallet funding, metadata activation, or further movements — will likely reveal whether this is the calm before a major wave, or simply a curious backend reshuffle. Disclaimer : This content is meant to inform and should not be considered financial advice. The views expressed in this article may include the author’s personal opinions and do not represent Times Tabloid’s opinion. Readers are urged to do in-depth research before making any investment decisions. Any action taken by the reader is strictly at their own risk. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. Follow us on Twitter , Facebook , Telegram , and Google News The post Over\\u202f40,000 Abnormal XRP Transactions Appear Out of Nowhere. Here’s What Happened appeared first on Times Tabloid .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Cryptocurrency|News|XRP|XRP Ledger', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764605225, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 67, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'timestabloid', 'NAME': 'TimesTabloid', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610928, 'CREATED_ON': 1664381507, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673235440}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 39, 'NAME': 'MINING', 'CATEGORY': 'MINING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 55, 'NAME': 'WALLET', 'CATEGORY': 'WALLET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55208866, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=224676', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764605110, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Price Plummets: Key Analysis as BTC Drops Below $84,000', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/bitcoin-price-drops-below-84000-6/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Bitcoin Price Plummets: Key Analysis as BTC Drops Below $84,000 The cryptocurrency market is experiencing a notable shift today as the Bitcoin price has fallen below the critical $84,000 threshold. According to real-time data from Binance’s USDT market, BTC is currently trading at $83,977.13. This movement has sent ripples through the trading community, prompting investors to ask: is this a minor correction or the start of a larger trend? Let’s break down the key factors behind this drop and what it could mean for your portfolio. What’s Driving the Current Bitcoin Price Action? Several factors can influence short-term Bitcoin price movements. While daily volatility is common, breaking through a psychological level like $84,000 often signals a shift in market sentiment. Typically, such moves are triggered by a combination of macroeconomic news, large sell orders (whale activity), or shifts in global liquidity. Understanding the ‘why’ behind the dip is the first step in making informed decisions. Key Levels to Watch After the Drop For traders, identifying support and resistance levels is crucial. Now that the Bitcoin price has moved below $84,000, analysts will be watching several key areas: Immediate Support: The zone around $83,500 could act as the first line of defense against further declines. Major Support: A stronger foundation may be found near the $82,000 level, which has been significant in recent weeks. Resistance Above: Any recovery will need to reclaim $84,500 and then $85,200 to suggest bullish momentum has returned. Monitoring these levels helps traders gauge market strength and potential reversal points. Is This a Buying Opportunity or a Time for Caution? Market pullbacks create divergent opinions. For some, a lower Bitcoin price represents a strategic entry point, especially for long-term holders who believe in the asset’s fundamentals. For others, it’s a warning sign to tighten stop-losses and reduce risk exposure. Your approach should align with your investment strategy: are you accumulating for the long haul, or trading short-term volatility? Actionable Insights for Crypto Investors Navigating price drops requires a clear plan. Here are practical steps to consider: Review Your Portfolio: Assess your current BTC allocation and ensure it still matches your risk tolerance. Avoid Emotional Decisions: Panic selling at a local low often leads to regret. Stick to your predefined strategy. Stay Informed: Follow reliable sources for updates on market sentiment and on-chain data, which can provide clues beyond the spot Bitcoin price . Consider Dollar-Cost Averaging (DCA): If you believe in long-term growth, systematic buying during dips can be an effective method. The Bigger Picture: Volatility is Part of the Journey It’s vital to remember that volatility is an inherent feature of cryptocurrency markets. While today’s Bitcoin price movement is significant, it occurs within the context of a larger, evolving asset class. Historical patterns show that Bitcoin has experienced numerous corrections on its path to new highs. Therefore, maintaining perspective is key for enduring the short-term turbulence. In summary, Bitcoin’s dip below $84,000 serves as a stark reminder of the market’s dynamic nature. By focusing on key technical levels, understanding the potential catalysts, and adhering to a disciplined strategy, investors can navigate this volatility. The current Bitcoin price action is not just a number on a screen; it’s a test of market structure and investor psychology. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Why did the Bitcoin price drop below $84,000? The drop is likely due to a combination of factors including profit-taking after a rally, negative macroeconomic sentiment, or large sell orders from institutional players. Specific news triggers can often accelerate these moves. Should I buy Bitcoin now that the price is lower? This depends entirely on your individual financial goals and risk tolerance. Some investors see dips as buying opportunities for long-term holdings, while traders might wait for confirmation of a support level before entering. How low could the Bitcoin price go? Predicting exact lows is impossible. However, traders watch key support levels like $83,500 and $82,000. A break below these could signal a deeper correction, while holding above them might indicate strength. Does this price drop affect the long-term outlook for Bitcoin? Short-term price movements rarely change the long-term fundamental thesis for proponents of Bitcoin. Many long-term investors view volatility as a normal characteristic of a maturing, yet still emerging, asset class. What is the best way to track the Bitcoin price? Use reputable cryptocurrency exchanges like Binance or Coinbase for real-time prices, and supplement with data from aggregate sites like CoinMarketCap or CoinGecko for a broader market view. Are other cryptocurrencies also dropping? Typically, when Bitcoin experiences a significant move, the rest of the crypto market (altcoins) often follows its lead, a phenomenon known as ‘market correlation.’ Found this analysis helpful? The crypto market moves fast, and knowledge is power. Share this article on your social media to help other investors stay informed and navigate the volatility with clarity. Let’s build a smarter community together! To learn more about the latest Bitcoin price trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Bitcoin institutional adoption. This post Bitcoin Price Plummets: Key Analysis as BTC Drops Below $84,000 first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BITCOIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Investment|Market Analysis|trading.', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1764605117, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1764610938, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55208867, 'GUID': 'https://coinpaprika.com/news/kraken-equity-incentives-program-institutions-launches', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1764605100, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/80/55208867.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Kraken Launches Market Participation Program', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'coinpap